                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Per CCR 249.3, this job control may be used to fill subsequent vacancies.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">The Pest Exclusion Branch, Exterior Program is recruiting to fill one (1) Plant Quarantine Supervisor I position located in Modoc County at the Alturas Border Protection Station.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">Under direction of the Agriculture Program Supervisor II (Area Manager), the Plant Quarantine Supervisor I (PQS I) is responsible for overseeing Plant Quarantine Inspectors (PQI), Agricultural Technicians, and Agricultural Aides on rotating shifts, maintaining operational consistency. The PQS I performs regulatory inspections on vehicles and commodities to prevent the introduction of unwanted pests into California and oversees contracted employees and non-State workers in the facility.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">The duties include, but are not limited to:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">• Oversee shift operations to ensure effective operations and to verify that all work is performed safely and accurately as prescribed by quarantine regulations, the Program operational guide, administrative manual, and other guides related to daily operations.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">• Manage and observe staff to ensure that proper safety and inspection techniques are employed and make immediate corrections if deficiencies are seen.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">• Inspect vehicles to determine if plant material (i.e., fruits, vegetables, plants, etc.) is present and to check the admissibility of plant material based on quarantine compliance and freedom from pests. This requires verbal communication and physical activities such as opening and removing containers, climbing, stooping, and bending around and within vehicles.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">• Provide feedback to employees regarding their job performance through the implementation of performance appraisals, meetings, and evaluations to encourage and assist staff to reach their career and promotional goals and subordinates staff in all aspects of plant quarantine work.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">• Communicate verbally and in writing (via e-mail, memos, and phone inquiries) with the public and government agencies regarding the purpose of regulating potential pest risk material, the purpose of inspections, and the solutions to quarantine issues.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">• Oversee maintenance of buildings and grounds to ensure the facility is safe, clean, and functional by assisting the Area Manager or Program Supervisor in preparing scopes of work and seeking out bids for contracts for services needed to maintain the facility and by performing safety inspections consistent with various State laws and regulations or Department policy.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">To be considered for this Plant Quarantine Supervisor I job opportunity, applicants must be either reachable on an employment list, have transfer eligibility, or have reinstatement eligibility.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><strong><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">Candidates may perform these essential functions with or without reasonable accommodation.</span></strong></p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=25655704&name=PlantQuarantineSupervisorIJC-453722Plant.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>

            <div id="pnlWorkingConditions">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Working Conditions</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">Employees in this classification are routinely assigned to work weekends and holidays, and rotating work shifts including day, evening, and night. This job is performed outdoors in the private vehicle and truck inspection areas approximately 60% of the time. The remaining time is spent in an office environment. When working outdoors, the employee may be exposed to high-low temperature changes, variable climatic conditions such as rain, snow, wind, fumes, and odors. The noise level in the work environment is moderate. The wearing of a uniform and use of safety equipment is required.</span></p>
                </p>
            
</div>
